   "body": "**Unblocked**: the `quote_only=1` capture #126 landed in #1139 (merged as 7a61018f; MANIFEST rows and HFR-PROTOCOL §6c « Batch A read-only captures »). The tap is now in scope: it opens the filtered view of the messages quoting this one, from the captured page, and never guesses.\n\n**Operator feedback (2026-11-18), added:**\n1. The bubble sits slightly too low. Raise it a little (`.quoted-bubble`, `reader.css:157-160`: today `margin: 0.25em 0 0 auto` in a `.trailer` aligned `flex-end`) so it aligns with the footer text line. State the value in the PR, with a before/after screenshot.\n2. It does not look tappable, which is true today: it is inert by design until #126. Once the tap is wired, give it a tappable affordance within Apple's behaviour (a 44 pt hit area, the press state of a link or button, an accessibility trait of a button labelled « Voir les N messages qui citent celui-ci »), with no custom effects.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
